WEBVTT

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.990
Yay, summer!

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.470
Yay, it's the beach!

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.270
You seem so excited.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:30.130
Well yeah! I bought a brand new swimsuit and floatie just for this!

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.160
Hooraayy!

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.760
Don't run! You're gonna trip!

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.110
Oh no, my floatie popped...

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.850
Hey now... Cheer up, okay?

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.570
Now it's all limp and saggy...

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.020
Where'd this freak downpour come from!?

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.340
Hotori!

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.590
No, I just bought that!

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.660
Hey, cover yourself!

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.280
As a high schooler...

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.870
No, as a woman...

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.010
As a human being, have some dignity!

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.980
My swimsuit!

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.140
C'mon, stop crying. I'll buy you some curry.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.990
One plate of curry please, Ma'am.

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:33.260
Sorry dear. Kitchen's closed for the day.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.570
Sheesh, what a crybaby.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.730
Mister Poorman!

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:15.460
You'll never amount to anything, Mister Poorman, so how about I treat you to a nice meal?

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.590
Mr. Richman is always such a jerk.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:20.720
But I'm hungry, so I guess I'll go.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.340
Wow!

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:27.290
If you put this picture under your pillow, you'll have a delicious dream.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.700
I start my mornings by taking Josephine for a walk.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.950
The early morning shopping district is nearly silent.

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:58.050
It's as if time has stopped for everyone but me-

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.300
Hey there! Good morning to ya!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.990
Seems like a freak typhoon's coming this way.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.830
Gonna rain cats and dogs tonight, they said.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:10.930
What'll I do? I'm in trouble!

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.940
I relish the quiet of the morning arcade.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.720
The early morning shopping district is very quiet-

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.290
Very quiet... Almost as if time has stopped for-

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.450
G'MORNIN!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.220
Heard there's a typhoon headed this way.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.580
Better make sure my veggies don't get blown away by the wind!

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:40.650
Well, considering how heavy they are, I think they'll be alright.

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.590
Oh, right... You've got a point.

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:51.770
As I walk the quiet streets each morning, I can forget about all the hustle and bustle.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.020
It's almost like my soul is cleansed anew.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.440
And right around this time each morning,

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:04.920
I exchange a simple greeting with the woman who jogs past me.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.660
Oh, good morning to you sir!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.480
Seems there's a freak typhoon coming our way.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:15.040
They say summer typhoons bring some heavy rain.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.670
I hope my house doesn't get damaged.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:19.900
Oh yes!

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.780
Oh yeah, I need to look through my survival kit. Hmm, non-perishable crackers are rock solid...

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:33.830
Then I buy some coffee from the usual vending machine and head back home.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:36.570
Huh?

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.940
The wind's wreaked havoc where I least expected it...

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.920
Are you trying to cheer me up, Josephine?

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.490
Okay, then let's head home.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.790
Back to our warm, happy home.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.100
What the!? It's been one thing after the other today!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.480
Hotori!

00:06:23.990 --> 00:06:28.020
So you went to pick up the paper while you were brushing and it got blown away, huh?

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.910
I hear there's a freak typhoon coming.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.490
Gotta watch out for the wind and rain.

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:39.710
Daddy, take us somewhere fun!

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.500
Yeah, like the beach or somewhere.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.590
Daddy doesn't have summer vacation like you do.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:48.010
How about you get your sister to take you to the public pool?

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.890
Don't be so selfish, you two!

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:55.490
Hotori, walk the dog for me this evening, okay?

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.690
I'm, like, kinda busy today, y'know...

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.440
My children all seem to take after their mother.

00:07:03.510 --> 00:07:07.690
My only true friend in this house is Josephine.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.390
Mister Poorman!

00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:13.700
Today, Mister Richman invited me out to catch insects.

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:18.330
Mister Poorman, you can put the beetles inside this golden cage.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.330
Hey, it escaped because there's only two bars!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.760
I had to lower the cost somehow.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:25.400
After all, it is made of gold!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.550
You're leaving too, Sis!?

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:35.870
What about the pool?

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.160
Why are you going to school during summer vacation?

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.660
Yeah, why? Tell me! Tell me!

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:43.940
Hey, why? Why're you going?

00:07:44.160 --> 00:07:45.940
Shut up!

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:49.900
I'm not going because I want to!

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:58.490
You don't have a care in the world, do you?

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:03.870
C'mon, what's the matter?

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.340
I was late even though I woke up early!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.850
Oh, I thought I was late, but I guess I'm the first one here!

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:25.020
You <i>are</i> late.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.610
Wait... Am I the only one in the class?

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:30.860
Whoa... Deja vu.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.140
Yes, this is the second time.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:34.610
Why are you late today?

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.660
You see, my dog seemed so very happy...

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:41.750
...So I thought I'd phrase my excuse in the form of a poem.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:46.000
And of course, you won't accept it.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.000
Okay, let's get on with it.

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.520
This is the final exam.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.760
And this is the make-up exam.

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:57.920
The make-up had exactly the same problems, just with different numbers.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.760
So how did you manage to get a worse score?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:02.220
I don't know what to tell you...

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:04.160
I guess it was just bad luck or something.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.900
I just kinda went with my gut.

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:08.150
Your gut!?

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.650
Did you just say "I went with my gut"?

00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:14.650
How dare you undermine the very foundation of math!

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:16.620
Not once have I ever heard that before.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:28.520
I've devised a method to get you to finally understand math.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.640
Devised?

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.170
Listen up, Arashiyama.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:34.670
Detective work is just like math!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:47.310
Yeah, I guess. They are vaguely related I suppose.

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:49.860
HEY! I'M BEING SERIOUS!

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:57.660
You see?  Basically, we try to find the culprit using the hints given.

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.700
We make inferences by consolidating what we already know.

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:06.000
And once you've removed all obstacles, the culprit's identity becomes clear.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.340
There is only one answer!

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.130
See? Just like a detective novel.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.640
I was getting carried away, I suppose.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:23.510
I got it!

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:27.090
Sleuthing is just like math!

00:10:27.090 --> 00:10:30.270
All of a sudden, I feel motivated!

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.560
You do?

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.250
Inspector Moriaki!

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.370
Well, if it isn't Arashiyama-kun!

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:51.200
Have you solved the case?

00:10:51.640 --> 00:10:55.500
Inspector, this horrifying case...

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.550
...can't be solved.

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.550
Agh! Oh God, the pain...

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:03.050
Ouch... it hurts...

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:09.810
I'm tired. I had to use my brain today.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.230
I was late 'cause I played with you.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.710
I think I'll take a nap after I walk you.

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.200
That's what summer's all about.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.250
Hey, we're not going that way.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:31.290
I'm walking YOU, remember?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:38.010
Don't just pick up everything you see!

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:39.970
You'll get a tummy ache.

00:11:45.780 --> 00:11:46.560
Dodo bird!

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.760
Fu-tard-ba!

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.440
Who're you callin' a tard!?

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:00.810
Hey, is THAT your dog?

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.700
Yep.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.320
Hey, Senpai!

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:08.080
It's rude to laugh at people's pets.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:09.700
Oh come on, look at it!

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:12.710
A racoon's walking another raccoon!

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:26.220
A raccoon... is walking... another...

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:30.390
Sic 'em, Josephine!

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:32.480
Tear them to shreds!

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:35.930
Josephine!?

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.230
Stop it! They're making fun of you!

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:48.220
...Hotori!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.180
Wake up, Hotori!

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:54.750
It seems I'm a raccoon, not a dog.

00:12:56.310 --> 00:12:59.080
I've decided to return to the mountains.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.630
Thanks for everything.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.860
Josephine?

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.260
I wish you the best.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:09.510
Josephine!? JOSEPHINE!

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:12.540
Jo-

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:23.830
Josephine!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.210
Josephine's gone...

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.970
She went back to the mountains!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:49.480
Josephine!

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.470
Josephiiine!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:58.770
You belong here with us! Come back home!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.070
Maybe she's pretending to be an actress.

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.900
That's just how girls are.

00:14:07.180 --> 00:14:07.990
Shake.

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:09.910
That means you do this.

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:13.660
If you can't even learn "shake", you'll get called a raccoon again.

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:15.910
Okay, let's try again. Shake!

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.790
This is hopeless.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:25.670
She has no clue what's going on.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:31.930
I've come to learn some things since I've lived here.

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.450
I think this family's hierarchy is like so.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:46.400
Maybe this is how Sensei feels when he tries to teach me math.

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:49.400
That's some food for thought.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:55.980
It seems that the only one below me is the very tall male.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.800
Mister Poorman.

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:04.540
Oh hi, Mister Poorman. I just bought a popular new DVD.

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.670
Would you like to come and see it in my home theater?

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:07.470
After all-

00:15:07.470 --> 00:15:09.930
I've got nothing to do and I've never seen it. I'll go.

00:15:10.400 --> 00:15:11.930
Oh, yes! Marvelous!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:14.890
That's a popular DVD for you!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:17.570
You don't have a DVD player?

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.210
I'm so cold...

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:25.320
Hi there, Mister Poorman. You look depressed as usual.

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:30.070
How about it? Would you care to visit my winter villa?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:30.850
Damn.

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:34.450
He really bugs me, but I'd just end up going back to my freezing cold house...Okay, I'll go.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.270
Okay, it's almost done.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.950
Give me a hand here, would you?

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.180
That's the ticket!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:00.180
Man, it's hot...

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.190
I wonder if they'll cancel the club meetings.

00:16:09.800 --> 00:16:10.940
Ooh, nice and cool.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.250
Eww, it's warm.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:53.130
She just snuck in and made herself at home.

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.640
Jeez, it's hot!

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.930
Here's your drink, my Queen.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.560
A sweet bun for you, my Queen.

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.310
This is the life!

00:17:23.880 --> 00:17:28.900
A torch for you, my Queen.

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.500
H-Hey guys, that's hot!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:34.170
I don't need a torch, okay?

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.530
Oops, I dropped it.

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:37.640
FIRE!

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.250
H-Hey, wait!

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.660
Oh no, I'm tangled up!

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:43.560
It burns!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.410
I can't move! Someone help me!

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:50.420
Fire on Mt. Pom-Pom...

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:00.680
How about Sashimi and Miso soup for dinner?

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.680
Huh? Weren't you going to make curry?

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:05.980
That's what I went shopping for originally,

00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:09.230
but the bald Fu Man Chu guy said to take some Sashimi.

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.230
Huh!? What in the world!?

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:15.740
Take with thee this Sashimi.

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.240
Maybe if you eat that Sashimi, you'll become immortal!

00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:25.100
Oh wait, by the Fu Man Chu guy, you meant Sanada's dad?

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:29.600
Hey, you know what I learned the other day?

00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:33.190
Omelette's taste really good if you add sugar!

00:18:33.190 --> 00:18:36.130
How have you been making them all this time?

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:39.130
You'd never think so, but it really is the secret to better taste!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.430
I know. Kinda like cooking sake, right?

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:44.060
What's so counterintuitive about that?

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:47.100
Hey, let's try putting some sugar in this too.

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.780
No way, forget it.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.260
Come on, it'll be yummy. I promise.

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:51.320
I said it's fine.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.850
Really, I'm not messing with you!

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:54.230
It doesn't need it.

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:55.650
Sweets can't be beat!

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:58.150
I said knock it off already.

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:04.530
Yikes...

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:10.040
If you're just gonna sit there, make up a song.

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.120
A song?

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:14.880
It's nice to listen to people sing live every now and then.

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:16.380
Okay then.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.220
Since we're going to the beach tomorrow,

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:23.720
I'll make up a beach-themed song.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:30.980
Seagulls sure are pretty.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.680
But crows sure aren't.

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:39.070
By: Johnny of the Docks.

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:42.330
No good?

00:19:42.840 --> 00:19:43.870
Not even close.

00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:48.320
Mister Poorman

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:51.310
Hi there.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:52.260
Ah, Mister Poorman.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:55.130
You look like you haven't had a decent meal for some time.

00:19:55.530 --> 00:20:00.260
I've perfected the ultimate Mixed Rice recipe. Care to come try it out?

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:01.200
Damn.

00:20:01.200 --> 00:20:04.890
He really bugs me, but I bet there's lots of great stuff inside it... I guess I'll go.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.170
I used a 60/40 mix of Koshihikari and Sasanishiki rice.

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:09.640
So there's nothing actually mixed in?

00:20:21.640 --> 00:20:23.970
What's up, Tatsuno-san?

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:24.910
You expecting someone?

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.410
N-No, not really...

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.160
Like the fishmonger's kid?

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.140
Hotori's not working today.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.210
And nobody else is here to interfere. It has to be today!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.710
I'm going to invite Sanada-kun to the beach!

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:47.550
Huh? Is Arashiyama off today?

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.310
She said she went to the beach. Just the two of them.

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:55.140
The beach!? The two of them!?

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.540
This can't be happening!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:21:01.920
While I was dragging my ass, Arashiyama went off to the beach with another guy!?

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.030
In that case, I've gotta hurry and confess. I've got nothing to lose!

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.950
If I get rejected, at least I can finally give up!

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:12.580
If I lose just because I was taking it too slow...

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:16.380
Now's my chance. I've gotta invite him right now!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:18.840
Would you like to go to the beach?

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:21.760
That's just 8 syllables, even with the question mark!

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.720
H-Hey, Sanada-kun...

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.090
Um... If you feel like it...

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.100
W-Would you...

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:32.750
Would you like to...

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.020
...go squid-watching?

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:39.270
Choked during the moment of truth...

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:41.780
Who cares about the beach!?

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:43.150
It's just a stupid beach!

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:46.530
I will darken the sea with my tears!

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.030
I wish I could stir the sea with my rage!

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:54.420
